{"title": "Sectional Mock #38 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>A sum of &#8377;4,620 is to be paid back in 2 equal annual installments. How much is each installment (in &#8377;) if the interest is compounded annually at 10% per annum?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#8377;4,620 &#2325;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 2 &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2346;&#2360; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; 10% &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340; (&#8377; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["2,420", "2,552", "2,662", "2,750"], "options_hi": ["2,420", "2,552", "2,662", "2,750"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let each instalment amount is &#8377;x.</p><p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=196 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19991/image055.png\"></p><p><img width=224 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19991/image056.png\"></p><p>4620 * 1.21 = x * 1.1 + x</p><p>2.1x = 4620 * 1.21</p><p>x = 2200 * 1.21</p><p>x = 2662</p><p>Hence, value of each instalment = &#8377;2662</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let each instalment amount is &#8377;x.</p><p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=196 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19991/image055.png\"></p><p><img width=224 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19991/image056.png\"></p><p>4620 * 1.21 = x * 1.1 + x</p><p>2.1x = 4620 * 1.21</p><p>x = 2200 * 1.21</p><p>x = 2662</p><p>Hence, value of each instalment = &#8377;2662</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p> A is 1.5 times efficient than B therefore takes 8 days less than B to complete a work. If A and B work on alternate days and A works on first day, then in how many days the work will be completed? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2360;&#2375; 1.5 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2369;&#2358;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2309;&#2340;&#2307; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; A, B &#2360;&#2375; 8 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2350; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2319;&#2325;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; A &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["17", "19", "19.5", "21"], "options_hi": ["17", "19", "19.5", "21"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "\"<p> Let time taken by A = x days</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/> Time taken by B = 1.5 x days</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/> 1.5x &#8211;x =8</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/> x = 16 days</p><p>1.5x = 24 days</p><p> Now, both work on alternate days </p><p> Work of 2 days = <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-001258.png\"/> </p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/> Work of 18 days = <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-002289.png\"/> </p><p> Remaining Work = <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-004263.png\"/> is done by A.</p><p> Time taken by A to complete <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-001257.png\"/> work <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000326.png\"/> = 1 day</p><p>Total work = (18+1)= 19 days</p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> Let time taken by A = x days</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/> Time taken by B = 1.5 x days</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/> 1.5x &#8211;x =8</p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/> x = 16 days</p><p>1.5x = 24 days</p><p> Now, both work on alternate days </p><p> Work of 2 days = <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-001258.png\"/> </p><p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/> Work of 18 days = <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-002289.png\"/> </p><p> Remaining Work = <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-004263.png\"/> is done by A.</p><p> Time taken by A to complete <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-001257.png\"/> work <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-000326.png\"/> = 1 day</p><p>Total work = (18+1)= 19 days</p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ashu can row 7.5 km an hour in still water. He finds that it takes four times as much time to row upstream, as it takes to row downstream. The speed of the stream is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2310;&#2358;&#2369; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 7.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2352;&#2347;&#2364;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2330;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2330;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2332;&#2364;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2342;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2330;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["3.5 km/h", "1.5 km/h", "4.5 km/h", "2.5 km/h"], "options_hi": ["3.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "1.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "4.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "2.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Speed of Ashu = 7.5 km/h</p><p>Let speed of stream = s km/h</p><p>Now,</p><p>4 * 1/(7.5 + s) = 1/(7.5  -  s)</p><p>4(7.5  -  s) = 7.5 + s</p><p>30  -  4s = 7.5 + s</p><p>5s = 22.5</p><p>s = 4.5</p><p>Hence, speed of stream = 4.5 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Speed of Ashu = 7.5 km/h</p><p>Let speed of stream = s km/h</p><p>Now,</p><p>4 * 1/(7.5 + s) = 1/(7.5  -  s)</p><p>4(7.5  -  s) = 7.5 + s</p><p>30  -  4s = 7.5 + s</p><p>5s = 22.5</p><p>s = 4.5</p><p>Hence, speed of stream = 4.5 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;Respective ratio of incomes of three persons A, B and C in Jan is&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2332;&#2344;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1", "options_en": ["Rs.45000", "Rs.30000", "Rs.60000", "Rs.72000"], "options_hi": ["45000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "30000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "60000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "72000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Respective ratio of incomes of A, B and C in Jan = <img width=276 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p12450/image002.gif\"></p><p>Let incomes of A, B and C in Jan be '7x', '5x' and '6x' respectively.</p><p>Respective ratio of incomes of A, B and C in Feb = 1: 1: 1</p><p>Let incomes of A, B and C in Feb be 'y', 'y' and 'y' respectively.</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>7x + 5x + 6x = y + y + y</p><p>18x = 3y</p><p>y = 6x</p><p>And,</p><p>7x  -  y = 5000</p><p>7x  -  6x = 5000</p><p>x = 5000</p><p>Total income of C in Jan and Feb together = 6x + y</p><p>= 6x + 6x</p><p>= 12x</p><p>= 12 * 5000</p><p>= Rs.60000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Respective ratio of incomes of A, B and C in Jan = <img width=276 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p12450/image002.gif\"></p><p>Let incomes of A, B and C in Jan be '7x', '5x' and '6x' respectively.</p><p>Respective ratio of incomes of A, B and C in Feb = 1: 1: 1</p><p>Let incomes of A, B and C in Feb be 'y', 'y' and 'y' respectively.</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>7x + 5x + 6x = y + y + y</p><p>18x = 3y</p><p>y = 6x</p><p>And,</p><p>7x  -  y = 5000</p><p>7x  -  6x = 5000</p><p>x = 5000</p><p>Total income of C in Jan and Feb together = 6x + y</p><p>= 6x + 6x</p><p>= 12x</p><p>= 12 * 5000</p><p>= Rs.60000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>A's capital is twice B's, and B's is three times C's. They invest these amounts for 8, 12 and 16 months respectively. If profit is Rs.170000, what is C's share?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2370;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2311;&#2344; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 8, 12 &#2324;&#2352; 16 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; 170000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; C &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.25600", "Rs.27200", "Rs.28400", "Rs.29600"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.25600", "&#2352;&#2369;.27200", "&#2352;&#2369;.28400", "&#2352;&#2369;.29600"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let C's capital = Y =&gt; B's capital = 3Y =&gt; A's capital = 6Y</p><p>Time - capital: A = 6Y X 8 = 48Y; B = 3Y X 12 = 36Y; C = Y X 16 = 16Y</p><p>Total = 48Y + 36Y + 16Y = 100Y</p><p>C's share = 170000  X  (16Y &div; 100Y) = 170000  X  0.16 = Rs. 27200</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let C's capital = Y =&gt; B's capital = 3Y =&gt; A's capital = 6Y</p><p>Time - capital: A = 6Y X 8 = 48Y; B = 3Y X 12 = 36Y; C = Y X 16 = 16Y</p><p>Total = 48Y + 36Y + 16Y = 100Y</p><p>C's share = 170000  X  (16Y &div; 100Y) = 170000  X  0.16 = Rs. 27200</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify: (&radic;(5 + 2&radic;6) + &radic;(5 &#8722; 2&radic;6))<sup>2</sup></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2352;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;: (&radic;(5 + 2&radic;6) + &radic;(5 &#8722; 2&radic;6))<sup>2</sup></p>", "options_en": ["8", "10", "12", "14"], "options_hi": ["8", "10", "12", "14"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let A = &radic;(5 + 2&radic;6) + &radic;(5 &#8722; 2&radic;6)</p><p>A<sup>2</sup> = (&radic;(5+2&radic;6))<sup>2</sup> + 2&radic;((5+2&radic;6)(5&#8722;2&radic;6)) + (&radic;(5&#8722;2&radic;6))<sup>2</sup></p><p>= (5 + 2&radic;6) + 2&radic;(25 &#8722; 24) + (5 &#8722; 2&radic;6)</p><p>= 5 + 2&radic;6 + 2&radic;1 + 5 &#8722; 2&radic;6</p><p>= 10 + 2</p><p>= 12</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let A = &radic;(5 + 2&radic;6) + &radic;(5 &#8722; 2&radic;6)</p><p>A<sup>2</sup> = (&radic;(5+2&radic;6))<sup>2</sup> + 2&radic;((5+2&radic;6)(5&#8722;2&radic;6)) + (&radic;(5&#8722;2&radic;6))<sup>2</sup></p><p>= (5 + 2&radic;6) + 2&radic;(25 &#8722; 24) + (5 &#8722; 2&radic;6)</p><p>= 5 + 2&radic;6 + 2&radic;1 + 5 &#8722; 2&radic;6</p><p>= 10 + 2</p><p>= 12</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>The table given here represents the distance (in km) travelled by two athletes P and Q in the same direction.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\" rowspan=\"2\"><b>Hour</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Distance travelled (in km)</b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>P</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Q</b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>1<sup>st</sup></b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">20</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">33</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>2<sup>nd</sup></b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">32</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">44</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>3<sup>rd</sup></b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">44</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">36</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>4<sup>th</sup></b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">23</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">30</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>5<sup>th</sup></b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">56</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">20</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>6<sup>th</sup></b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">18</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">15</td></tr></table><p>Q's average speed (km/hr) during the last five hours is : </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2379; &#2319;&#2341;&#2354;&#2368;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; (&#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\" rowspan=\"2\">&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\" colspan=\"2\">&#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; (&#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;)</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">P</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Q</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">1<sup>st</sup></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">20</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">33</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2<sup>nd</sup></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">32</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">44</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">3<sup>rd</sup></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">44</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">36</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">4<sup>&#2357;&#2366;&#2306;</sup></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">23</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">30</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">5<sup>&#2357;&#2366;&#2306;</sup></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">56</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">20</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">6<sup>th</sup></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">18</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">15</td></tr></table><p>&#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2306;&#2330; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344; Q &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; (&#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;) &#2361;&#2376;: </p>", "options_en": ["22 km/hr", "35 km/hr", "30 km/hr", "Cannot be determined"], "options_hi": ["22 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "35 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "30 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "&#2340;&#2351; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Only distance are given we cannot find the speed.</p><p>Cannot be determined.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Only distance are given we cannot find the speed.</p><p>Cannot be determined.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the surface area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of a sphere of diameter 28 cm. (Use &#960; = 22/7)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>28 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;2 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; (&#960; = 22/7 &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;)</p>", "options_en": ["1731", "2464", "2856", "1724"], "options_hi": ["1731", "2464", "2856", "1724"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Diameter = 28 cm</p><p>Radius r = 28/2 = 14 cm</p><p>Surface area of sphere = 4 * (22/7) * 14 * 14 = 88 * 28 = 2464 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Diameter = 28 cm</p><p>Radius r = 28/2 = 14 cm</p><p>Surface area of sphere = 4 * (22/7) * 14 * 14 = 88 * 28 = 2464 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the positions of the digits of a two digit number are interchanged, the number obtained is smaller than the original number by 27. If the digits of the number are in the ratio of 2 : 1 then what is the original number?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; 27 &#2325;&#2350; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 2 : 1 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["48", "36", "63", "74"], "options_hi": ["48", "36", "63", "74"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the original number be = 10a + b</p><p>According to the question; 10a + b = 10b + a + 27</p><p>=&gt; 9a = 9b + 27</p><p>=&gt; a = b + 3... (1)</p><p>According to the question; a/b=2/1</p><p>=&gt; a = 2b... (2)</p><p>From Equation (1) and (2) we will get;</p><p>=&gt; 2b = b + 3</p><p>=&gt; b = 3</p><p>Hence; a = 6</p><p>Therefore original number = 63</p><p></p><p><b> Express Method </b></p><p>By checking options,</p><p>48 - 84 = -36 (not correct)</p><p>36 - 63 = -27 (not correct)</p><p>63 - 36 = 27. (Correct)</p><p>Hence original number = 63</p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the original number be = 10a + b</p><p>According to the question; 10a + b = 10b + a + 27</p><p>=&gt; 9a = 9b + 27</p><p>=&gt; a = b + 3... (1)</p><p>According to the question; a/b=2/1</p><p>=&gt; a = 2b... (2)</p><p>From Equation (1) and (2) we will get;</p><p>=&gt; 2b = b + 3</p><p>=&gt; b = 3</p><p>Hence; a = 6</p><p>Therefore original number = 63</p><p></p><p><b> Express Method </b></p><p>By checking options,</p><p>48 - 84 = -36 (not correct)</p><p>36 - 63 = -27 (not correct)</p><p>63 - 36 = 27. (Correct)</p><p>Hence original number = 63</p><p></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>In nine innings of cricket, the average of a batsman is 58 runs. How many runs does he need to make in the tenth innings to get the average score 61?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2380; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2375;&#2348;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; 58 &#2352;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2352; 61 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2360;&#2357;&#2368;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2352;&#2344; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["88", "69", "79", "100"], "options_hi": ["88", "69", "79", "100"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Total runs in nine innings = 9 * 58</p><p>Total runs in ten innings = 10 * 61</p><p>Runs scored in 10<sup>th</sup> innings = 10 * 61  -  9 * 58</p><p>= 610  -  522</p><p>= 88</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total runs in nine innings = 9 * 58</p><p>Total runs in ten innings = 10 * 61</p><p>Runs scored in 10<sup>th</sup> innings = 10 * 61  -  9 * 58</p><p>= 610  -  522</p><p>= 88</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>In how much time (in years, rounded off to 2 decimal places) will &#8377;10,800 amount to &#8377;24,800 if invested at simple interest at the rate of 15.5% per annum?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; (&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, 2 &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;) 10,800 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; 24,800 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; 15.5% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;?", "options_en": ["7.72", "8.36", "9.54", "6.89"], "options_hi": ["7.72", "8.36", "9.54", "6.89"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Principal = 10800</p><p>Amount= 24800</p><p>Rate= 15.5%</p><p>Ineterest = 24800  -  10800 =14000</p><p>14000 = 10800*15.5*T/100</p><p>T= 14000/(108*15.5)=8.36</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Principal = 10800</p><p>Amount= 24800</p><p>Rate= 15.5%</p><p>Ineterest = 24800  -  10800 =14000</p><p>14000 = 10800*15.5*T/100</p><p>T= 14000/(108*15.5)=8.36</p><p>Option (b) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>A kite is flying in the sky with its string fully extended to 318 m, making an angle of 45&deg; with the ground. Find the height (in m) at which the kite is flying.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2340;&#2306;&#2327; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2337;&#2379;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; 318 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2347;&#2376;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; &#2310;&#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2337;&#2364; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2332;&#2364;&#2350;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; 45&deg; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2340;&#2306;&#2327; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; (&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2337;&#2364; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["318&radic;2", "106&radic;3", "318&radic;3", "159&radic;2"], "options_hi": ["318&radic;2", "106&radic;3", "318&radic;3", "159&radic;2"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=201 height=98 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27478/image004.png\"></p><p>AC = Length of string</p><p>AB = height at which the kite is flying</p><p>sin 45&deg; = AB/AC</p><p>1/&radic;2 = AB/ 318</p><p>AB = 159&radic;2 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=201 height=98 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27478/image004.png\"></p><p>AC = Length of string</p><p>AB = height at which the kite is flying</p><p>sin 45&deg; = AB/AC</p><p>1/&radic;2 = AB/ 318</p><p>AB = 159&radic;2 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Height & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the number of arrangements if a dice rolled 44 times?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366; 44 &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2369;&#2338;&#2364;&#2325;&#2366; &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["6<sup>22</sup>", "6<sup>44</sup>", "6<sup>43</sup>", "6<sup>45</sup>"], "options_hi": ["6<sup>22</sup>", "6<sup>44</sup>", "6<sup>43</sup>", "6<sup>45</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>When a dic e rolled N times, the number of arrangements = 6<sup>N</sup></p><p>Number of arrangements if a die rolled 44 times = 6<sup>44</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>When a dic e rolled N times, the number of arrangements = 6<sup>N</sup></p><p>Number of arrangements if a die rolled 44 times = 6<sup>44</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of &radic;192 + &radic;432  -  &radic;588  -  &radic;108?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&radic;192 + &radic;432 - &radic;588 - &radic;108 &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["2&radic;2", "4&radic;3", "&radic;3", "0"], "options_hi": ["2&radic;2", "4&radic;3", "&radic;3", "0"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Here, &radic;192 + &radic;432  -  &radic;588  -  &radic;108</p><p>= &radic;(8 * 8 * 3) + &radic;(12 * 12 * 3)  -  &radic;(14 * 14 * 3)  -  &radic;(6 * 6 * 3)</p><p>= 8&radic;3 + 12&radic;3  -  14&radic;3  -  6&radic;3</p><p>= 20&radic;3  -  20&radic;3</p><p>= <b>0</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here, &radic;192 + &radic;432  -  &radic;588  -  &radic;108</p><p>= &radic;(8 * 8 * 3) + &radic;(12 * 12 * 3)  -  &radic;(14 * 14 * 3)  -  &radic;(6 * 6 * 3)</p><p>= 8&radic;3 + 12&radic;3  -  14&radic;3  -  6&radic;3</p><p>= 20&radic;3  -  20&radic;3</p><p>= <b>0</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three pipes, A, B, C can fill an empty cistern in 2, 3 and 6 hours, respectively. They are opened together. After what time should B be closed, so that the cistern gets filled in exactly 1 hr 15 min?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;, A, B, C &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 2, 3 &#2324;&#2352; 6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325;&#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; B &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2306;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2367; 1 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; 15 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2306;&#2337; &#2349;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["30 min", "20 min", "45 min", "15 min"], "options_hi": ["30 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "20 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "45 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "15 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let B should be closed in T hours.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>1.25(1/A + 1/C) + T/B = 1</p><p>=&gt; 1.25(1/2 + 1/6) + T/3 = 1</p><p>=&gt; T/3 = 1  -  5/6 = 1/6</p><p>=&gt; T = 3/6 = &frac12; hour</p><p>=&gt; T = 30 minutes</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let B should be closed in T hours.</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>1.25(1/A + 1/C) + T/B = 1</p><p>=&gt; 1.25(1/2 + 1/6) + T/3 = 1</p><p>=&gt; T/3 = 1  -  5/6 = 1/6</p><p>=&gt; T = 3/6 = &frac12; hour</p><p>=&gt; T = 30 minutes</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>If tan&#952; = 21/20, then what is the value of (3cos&#952;  -  2sin&#952;)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; tan&#952; = 21/20, &#2340;&#2379; (3cos&#952; - 2sin&#952;) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["12/29", "20/29", "18/29", "21/29"], "options_hi": ["12/29", "20/29", "18/29", "21/29"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>tan&#952; = 21/20</p><p>Perpendicular = 21, Base = 20</p><p>Hypotenuse = &radic;(21<sup>2</sup> + 20<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= &radic;(441 + 400)</p><p>= 29</p><p>Now,</p><p>3cos&#952;  -  2sin&#952; = 3*20/29  -  2*21/29</p><p>= 18/29</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>tan&#952; = 21/20</p><p>Perpendicular = 21, Base = 20</p><p>Hypotenuse = &radic;(21<sup>2</sup> + 20<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= &radic;(441 + 400)</p><p>= 29</p><p>Now,</p><p>3cos&#952;  -  2sin&#952; = 3*20/29  -  2*21/29</p><p>= 18/29</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>A milkman has three different qualities of milk. 517 gallons of 1st quality, 611 gallons of 2nd quality and 706 gallons of 3rd quality. Find the least possible number of bottles of equal size in which different milk of different qualities can be filled without mixing.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 517 &#2327;&#2376;&#2354;&#2344;, &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 611 &#2327;&#2376;&#2354;&#2344; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 706 &#2327;&#2376;&#2354;&#2344;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2379;&#2340;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2348;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319; &#2349;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["39", "37", "41", "33"], "options_hi": ["39", "37", "41", "33"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>First quality = 517 Gallons, Second quality = 611 Gallons, Third quality = 705 Gallons</p><p>The least number of bottles will be in the size of HCF of 517, 611, and 705.</p><p>Now,</p><p>517 = 47 x 11</p><p>611 = 47 x 13</p><p>705 = 47 x 15</p><p>HCF = 47</p><p>So, required number of bottles = 11 + 13 + 15 = 39</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>First quality = 517 Gallons, Second quality = 611 Gallons, Third quality = 705 Gallons</p><p>The least number of bottles will be in the size of HCF of 517, 611, and 705.</p><p>Now,</p><p>517 = 47 x 11</p><p>611 = 47 x 13</p><p>705 = 47 x 15</p><p>HCF = 47</p><p>So, required number of bottles = 11 + 13 + 15 = 39</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>A wheel makes 700 revolutions to cover a distance of 77 kilometres. What will be the diameter of the wheel?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2361;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; 77 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 700 &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2361;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["25 m", "30 m", "20 m", "35 m"], "options_hi": ["25 &#2350;&#2368;", "30 &#2350;&#2368;", "20 &#2350;&#2368;", "35 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Distance covered by wheel in 1 revolution = &#960;*diameter</p><p>Therefore distance covered in 700 revolutions = 700* &#960;*diameter</p><p>According to question, 700* &#960;*diameter = 77*1000</p><p>Diameter = 77*1000*7/(22*700) = 35 m</p><p>Hence, the diameter of wheel is 35 m.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Distance covered by wheel in 1 revolution = &#960;*diameter</p><p>Therefore distance covered in 700 revolutions = 700* &#960;*diameter</p><p>According to question, 700* &#960;*diameter = 77*1000</p><p>Diameter = 77*1000*7/(22*700) = 35 m</p><p>Hence, the diameter of wheel is 35 m.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three men, four women and six children can complete a work in seven days. A woman does double the work a man does and children does half the work a man does. How many women alone can complete this work in 7 days?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359;, &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2331;&#2361; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2366;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; 7 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["7", "8", "12", "Cannot be determined"], "options_hi": ["7", "8", "12", "&#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let 1 woman's 1 day's work = x</p><p>Then, 1 man's 1 day's work = &#119909;/2 and 1 child&#8242;s 1 day work = x/4</p><p>So, (3&#119909;/2 + 4&#119909; + 6&#119909;/4) = 1/7</p><p>x = 1/7 * 4/28 = 1/49</p><p>1 woman alone can complete the work in 49 days.</p><p>So, to complete the work in 7 days, number of women required = (49/7) = 7</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let 1 woman's 1 day's work = x</p><p>Then, 1 man's 1 day's work = &#119909;/2 and 1 child&#8242;s 1 day work = x/4</p><p>So, (3&#119909;/2 + 4&#119909; + 6&#119909;/4) = 1/7</p><p>x = 1/7 * 4/28 = 1/49</p><p>1 woman alone can complete the work in 49 days.</p><p>So, to complete the work in 7 days, number of women required = (49/7) = 7</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>A well with 14 cm radius is dug 23 cm deep. Find the volume of the earth taken out of it.</p>", "q_hi": "14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2369;&#2310;&#2305; 23 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2327;&#2361;&#2352;&#2366; &#2326;&#2379;&#2342;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2350;&#2367;&#2335;&#2381;&#2335;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["14,178 cm<sup>3</sup>", "14,108 cm<sup>3</sup>", "14,168 cm<sup>3</sup>", "15,168 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["14,178 cm<sup>3</sup>", "14,108 cm<sup>3</sup>", "14,168 cm<sup>3</sup>", "15,168 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of the cylinder = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h</p><p>=&gt;&#960;  X  14<sup>2</sup>  X  23 = (22/7)  X  196  X  23</p><p>=&gt; 22  X  28  X  23 = 14168 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of the cylinder = &#960;r<sup>2</sup>h</p><p>=&gt;&#960;  X  14<sup>2</sup>  X  23 = (22/7)  X  196  X  23</p><p>=&gt; 22  X  28  X  23 = 14168 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;In the given figure AB and CD intersect at T and ET is perpendicular at line AB. If &#8736;ATC = <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>7", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2310;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; AB &#2324;&#2352; CD, T &#2346;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375;&#2342; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; ET &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; AB &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#8736;ATC = <div style='display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;'><span style='text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;'>7", "options_en": ["145&deg;", "135&deg;", "125&deg;", "115&deg;"], "options_hi": ["145&deg;", "135&deg;", "125&deg;", "115&deg;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>ET is perpendicular at line AB.</p><p>So, &#8736;BTE = 90&deg;</p><p>So, &#8736;ATE = 90&deg;</p><p>Let &#8736;ATC = 7x an &#8736;CTE = 11x</p><p>Thus, 7x + 11x = 90&deg;</p><p>=&gt; x = 5</p><p>Hence, &#8736;ATC = 35&deg; and &#8736;CTE = 55&deg;</p><p>By line property,</p><p>&#8736;DTA + &#8736;ATC = 180&deg;</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;DTA = 180&deg;  -  35&deg;</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;DTA = 145&deg;</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>ET is perpendicular at line AB.</p><p>So, &#8736;BTE = 90&deg;</p><p>So, &#8736;ATE = 90&deg;</p><p>Let &#8736;ATC = 7x an &#8736;CTE = 11x</p><p>Thus, 7x + 11x = 90&deg;</p><p>=&gt; x = 5</p><p>Hence, &#8736;ATC = 35&deg; and &#8736;CTE = 55&deg;</p><p>By line property,</p><p>&#8736;DTA + &#8736;ATC = 180&deg;</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;DTA = 180&deg;  -  35&deg;</p><p>=&gt; &#8736;DTA = 145&deg;</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two bullets were fired at a place at an interval of 38 minutes. A person approaching the firing point in his car hears the two sounds at an interval of 36 minutes. The speed of sound is 330m/s. What is the speed of car(in km/hr)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>38 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2366;&#2354; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2330;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312;&#2306; &#2341;&#2368;&#2306;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375;&#2348;&#2366;&#2395;&#2368; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2346;&#2361;&#2369;&#2305;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 36 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;&#2366;&#2354; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2343;&#2381;&#2357;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2360;&#2369;&#2344;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2343;&#2381;&#2357;&#2344;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 330 &#2350;&#2368;/&#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; (&#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["60", "68", "72", "66"], "options_hi": ["60", "68", "72", "66"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Distance travelled by the man in 36 minutes is equal to the distance travelled by sound in (38  -  36) = 2 minutes.</p> <p>Now let the speed of the car be s km/hr.</p> <p>s x 36/60 = 330 x 18/5 x 2/60</p> <p>=&gt; s = 66 x 18 x 2/36 = 66 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Distance travelled by the man in 36 minutes is equal to the distance travelled by sound in (38  -  36) = 2 minutes.</p> <p>Now let the speed of the car be s km/hr.</p> <p>s x 36/60 = 330 x 18/5 x 2/60</p> <p>=&gt; s = 66 x 18 x 2/36 = 66 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the equation of a line passing through point P(3, 4) and parallel to the line 4x + 2y  -  2 = 0.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; P(3, 4) &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379;&#2325;&#2352; &#2327;&#2369;&#2332;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; 4x + 2y - 2 = 0 &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2x + y  -  10 = 0", "x + 2y  -  6 = 0", "3x + y  -  12 = 0", "2x + 3y  -  8 = 0"], "options_hi": ["2x + y - 10 = 0", "x + 2y - 6 = 0", "3x + y - 12 = 0", "2x + 3y - 8 = 0"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>In the given equation of the line: 4x + 2y  -  2 = 0</p><p>y = -2x + 1</p><p>Here, slope = -2</p><p>Now, equation of line passing through P(3, 4) and slope (-2) is:</p><p>(y  -  4) = (-2)(x  -  3)</p><p><b>2x + y  -  10 = 0</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In the given equation of the line: 4x + 2y  -  2 = 0</p><p>y = -2x + 1</p><p>Here, slope = -2</p><p>Now, equation of line passing through P(3, 4) and slope (-2) is:</p><p>(y  -  4) = (-2)(x  -  3)</p><p><b>2x + y  -  10 = 0</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>HCF and LCM of two numbers are 13 and 156 respectively. If one of the two numbers are 26, then find the other number.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; HCF &#2324;&#2352; LCM &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 13 &#2324;&#2352; 156 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; 26 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["70", "64", "78", "88"], "options_hi": ["70", "64", "78", "88"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the other number = b</p><p>LCM * HCF = Product of two numbers</p><p>13 * 156 = 26 * b</p><p>b = (13 * 156)/26</p><p>b = 78</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the other number = b</p><p>LCM * HCF = Product of two numbers</p><p>13 * 156 = 26 * b</p><p>b = (13 * 156)/26</p><p>b = 78</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify:</p><p><img width=199 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image066.png\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p><p><img width=199 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image066.png\"></p>", "options_en": ["0", "1", "-1", "2"], "options_hi": ["0", "1", "-1", "2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=199 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image066.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image067.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image068.png\"></p><p><img width=24 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image069.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=199 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image066.png\"></p><p><img width=117 height=41 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image067.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image068.png\"></p><p><img width=24 height=16 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25685/image069.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}]}